 "ios-actions|Context menus": {
  "summary": "A Plenix context menu on iOS is the system context menu (UIContextMenuInteraction), kept native in behavior: a touch and hold or a secondary click opens it, a lifted preview confirms the target, the background dims and VoiceOver reads the actions. Plenix decides what it holds: only the commands that apply to that item, at most three groups, the most used nearest the item, destructive items last and marked, and every command also reachable in the main interface. The system draws the menu and its glass; where Plenix draws a menu itself it uses the Plenix menu tokens shown in the Plenix rows, and the preview keeps the item’s own shape.",
